lem-bw-implies-archimedean	lemma	"Bolzano-Weierstrass alone forces the Archimedean property, so it needs no separate Archimedean hypothesis"
Let $F$ be an ordered field with the Bolzano-Weierstrass property (BW) of [[def-completeness-properties]]. Then $F$ is Archimedean ([[def-archimedean-field]]). Consequently (BW) needs no Archimedean hypothesis attached to it, in contrast with the nested interval property and with Cauchy completeness, which do ([[fs-nested-intervals-implies-lub]], [[fs-cauchy-complete-implies-lub]]).
