lem-point-filters-are-dense-in-the-minimal-cauchy-filter-space	lemma	"The minimal Cauchy filters associated to points define a uniformly continuous dense canonical map"
The map $\eta:X\to\widehat X$ sending $x$ to the minimal Cauchy filter associated to its principal filter is uniformly continuous and has dense image.
