thm-hausdorff-completion-of-a-uniform-space	theorem	"Every uniform space has a complete Hausdorff reflection with dense canonical image, and the canonical map is a uniform embedding exactly when the original uniformity is separated"
Every uniform space $X$ has a Hausdorff completion $\eta:X\to\widehat X$. The map has dense image, and it is a uniform embedding if and only if the original uniformity is separated.
