lem-completely-regular-topologies-come-from-continuous-pseudometrics	lemma	"The topology of a completely regular space is induced by the gauge of its continuous $[0,1]$-valued pseudometrics"
The topology of a completely regular space is induced by the gauge of pseudometrics $p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)|$, where $f:X\to[0,1]$ ranges over continuous maps.
