thm-topological-group-uniformities-induce-the-given-topology	theorem	"The left and right uniformities of a topological group induce its topology, and inversion interchanges them"
The left and right uniformities of a topological group induce its given topology. Inversion is a uniform isomorphism from the left uniformity to the right uniformity.
